<title>USA: Clinton talks on veto will go into weekend.</title>
<headline>Clinton talks on veto will go into weekend.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton's deliberations on whether to use the line-item veto to strike some special interest tax breaks from the new budget plan will extend into the weekend, the White House said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Spokesman Mike McCurry said Clinton would have an initial meeting on a short list of possible veto targets later on Thursday. These deliberations will continue into the weekend as Clinton faces a Monday deadline to act, McCurry said.</p>
</text>
